cff-version: 1.2.0

message: "Please cite this repository when using its experimental evidence, verification artefacts, results, or supporting documentation. The repository-level metadata describes the research evidence repository as a whole; the maintained v1.0.0 and v1.1.0 evidence-release labels are identified below."

title: "ML-KEM CBMC Verification Case-Study Evidence"

type: dataset

authors:
  - given-names: "Girish"
    family-names: "Nallan Chakravathy"

repository-code: "https://github.com/Girish2052003/girish-nallan-chakravathy-thesis-2026-mlkem-cbmc-verification-case-study-evidences"

url: "https://github.com/Girish2052003/girish-nallan-chakravathy-thesis-2026-mlkem-cbmc-verification-case-study-evidences"

date-released: "2026-07-19"

abstract: "A versioned research evidence repository supporting an MSc thesis case study on AI-assisted formal verification of selected ML-KEM implementation components with CBMC. The repository preserves property-verification harnesses, assumptions, CBMC commands and outputs, mutation and negative-control results, source-revision records, manifests, checksums, reports, provenance records, and supporting scientific documentation. The maintained release snapshot is addressed by v1.0.0 for the V5 baseline evidence role and by v1.1.0 for the expanded RQ2 evidence role. The two release tags share that maintained snapshot while later main-branch development may advance independently."

keywords:
  - "ML-KEM"
  - "CBMC"
  - "formal verification"
  - "post-quantum cryptography"
  - "C verification"
  - "verification evidence"
  - "bounded model checking"
  - "research reproducibility"

